# Stronger, Wider and Lingering Cloth Waves

Status: DONE
Milestone: M38 A visibly stronger mouse response with a longer natural decay
Dependencies: 41_LONGER_RED_STRIPED_SUPPORTED_AWNING.todo

## Purpose

The owner wants the cloth much more sensitive to the mouse, with waves spreading
farther and lingering after input stops. This changes page-cloth interaction only.

## Tasks

- [x] Preserve the prior model and renderer for controlled comparison.
- [x] Increase mouse forcing/compliance and broaden the influence patch.
- [x] Strengthen neighbour coupling and reduce damping while retaining finite bounds.
- [x] Preserve exact rail/edge pins, rigid supports, static restoration and idle stopping.
- [x] Compare displacement, propagation width and decay against the actual prior model.
- [x] Check the actual uploaded browser mesh and full interaction safeguards.
- [x] Publish the scoped motion-only modules/cache HTML and update documentation.

## Acceptance criteria

- Clearly stronger initial response and wider wave propagation, not only faster timing.
- A visible lingering tail, followed by exact idle rather than permanent animation.
- Fixed metal/rails, 20px draw gutter, approximately2Mpixel budget and all safe fallbacks.
- Static artwork, dimensions, canopy colour, phone tilt and all other UI remain unchanged.
- No new image views, questions or invented aesthetic approval.

